Room: extension update checks only when the host asks.

Room makes no request the user did not ask for. Once an extension is
installed its update check is such a request, made on the host's timer
(once a day while an extension is installed, never otherwise) through
ExtensionUpdater::CheckNow. Room's network policy passes
--disable-background-networking, which ChromeExtensionsBrowserClient turns
into "no extension update checks at all", so the host's check would be
refused too; without the switch Chrome's own schedule (a check at startup and
every five hours) would run.

No existing hook: IsBackgroundUpdateAllowed() reads the process-wide switch,
which other services also read (variations, translate, the intranet redirect
detector), so it cannot be dropped; the ExtensionsBrowserClient is a
process-wide singleton Chrome owns. //room answers true only inside the
host's CheckNow call (the checks start synchronously there); Chrome's own
scheduled checks, an extension's runtime.requestUpdateCheck and policy
re-checks are refused.

Phase 3.6a, 2026-10-05. //room: room/core/room_extensions.mm.
diff --git a/chrome/browser/extensions/chrome_extensions_browser_client.cc b/chrome/browser/extensions/chrome_extensions_browser_client.cc
index 0f89eff019706..a26d4dd5c3c35 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/extensions/chrome_extensions_browser_client.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/extensions/chrome_extensions_browser_client.cc
@@ -164,6 +164,12 @@
 #include "chrome/common/extensions/manifest_handlers/settings_overrides_handler.h"
 #endif
 
+namespace room {
+// Room: set by //room/core at startup. Extension update checks (the
+// ExtensionUpdater's and update_client's) run only while it returns true.
+bool (*g_extension_update_allowed_hook)() = nullptr;
+}  // namespace room
+
 namespace extensions {
 
 namespace {
@@ -607,6 +613,9 @@ ExtensionCache* ChromeExtensionsBrowserClient::GetExtensionCache() {
 }
 
 bool ChromeExtensionsBrowserClient::IsBackgroundUpdateAllowed() {
+  if (::room::g_extension_update_allowed_hook) {
+    return ::room::g_extension_update_allowed_hook();
+  }
   return !base::CommandLine::ForCurrentProcess()->HasSwitch(
       ::switches::kDisableBackgroundNetworking);
 }
